From 403c279f9c828220ba088f677842bb0378a297fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OneFeiFan <3022504358@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:18:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] config: enable ZRAM_WRITEBACK
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Enable zram writeback to a backing block device. Generic upstream
feature; on Xiaomi devices PerfInit uses it to attach the ExtM backing
device (/data/extm/extm_file via dm-linear) before setting the disk
size, and xiaomi/0027 builds the ExtM writeback logic on top of it.

Origin: 本地配置
Upstream-Status: Not-Applicable
KABI: none
Depends-On: 0016 内建 zram
Tested-On: yudi 5.10.272（PerfInit 建立写回设备 dm-48）, 2026-10-31

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
index e1c86a8f5..4b8025a84 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
@@ -483,6 +483,8 @@ CONFIG_DM_UEVENT=y
 CONFIG_DM_VERITY=y
 CONFIG_DM_VERITY_FEC=y
 CONFIG_DM_BOW=y
+# yudi: zram writeback (Xiaomi ExtM probe)
+CONFIG_ZRAM_WRITEBACK=y
 CONFIG_NETDEVICES=y
 CONFIG_DUMMY=y
 CONFIG_WIREGUARD=y
-- 
2.43.0

